# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in the working tree on all 3 OSes.
# The checkout is deliberately not platform-native: a native checkout leaves the
# tree half CRLF (what git wrote) and half LF (what editors and xtask wrote), and
# CRLF reaching a .sh on Linux/macOS shows up as `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`.
# eol=lf here outranks whatever core.autocrlf a developer has set locally, so the
# tree is byte-identical everywhere. Keeps fmt/clippy/CI consistent across 3 OSes.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.rs text
*.toml text
*.md text
*.qml text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.ps1 text
*.sh text eol=lf

# Captured raw git output for parser tests: byte-exact, never re-encoded.
*.bin binary
